            "body": "> > Does :imap  show the mapping from 'mini.pairs'?\r\n> \r\n> Yes, it shows:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> i  <Space>     * v:lua.MiniPairs.open(\"  \", \"%$%$\")\r\n>                  Open action for \"  \" pair\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> But I can't get the auto spacing work. I'm on neovim 0.10.1\r\n\r\nI am not sure what to tell here. With this mapping for `<Space>` in Insert mode it should turn `$$` into `$  $` when pressing `<Space>` in between `$$`. Just like in demo.\r\n\r\nI guess the best suggestion is to try reproducing with only 'mini.pairs' enabled. It should not reproduce. And after that try bisecting the config until you find the relevant part that makes it work as you see.",
