        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@aik2mlj I also ran into this issue with spaces. For me it was because of [this](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/ecfaed3cc1cbe3013f1201594adde2ea0022c455/lua/lazyvim/util/mini.lua#L149-L150) and [this](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/ecfaed3cc1cbe3013f1201594adde2ea0022c455/lua/lazyvim/plugins/coding.lua#L121) in LazyVim. I managed to fix this by removing `$` from the `skip_next` pattern:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.pairs\",\r\n  opts = {\r\n    skip_next = [=[[%w%%%'%[%\"%.%`]]=],\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nand this was my config:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal pairs = require(\"mini.pairs\")\r\npairs.map_buf(bufnr, \"i\", \" \", { action = \"open\", pair = \"  \", neigh_pattern = \"%$%$\" })\r\npairs.map_buf(bufnr, \"i\", \"$\", { action = \"closeopen\", pair = \"$$\" })\r\n```",
